course: dictionary
lesson: 8380
title: Short forms and website endings
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A short form is a few letters that stand for a longer thing. On the internet, the ending of a web address is a clue to where the site comes from. «The site ended in .ru, so it is a website from Russia.» Always look at the ending before you click on a link you do not know.
explain: On its own, ru is not a real word. It is a fragment, a small piece of a bigger word or code. In «February», you can hear the r-u sound in your head, even though many people skip the r when they speak. Breaking words into pieces helps you spell them.
explain: RU is also a short code for Russia or the Russian language, so you will see it on maps, forms and in lists of languages. Check the meaning from the words around it, just as you do with any unknown word.
fact: A domain ending is the last part of a web address, such as .com, .uk or .ru.
fact: .ru is the domain ending for websites from Russia.
fact: RU or ru is a short code for Russia or the Russian language.
fact: ru is a fragment, not a word you can use by itself in a sentence.
fact: Check an unknown link before you click, and look at its ending to see where it comes from.
exercise: What does the ending .ru tell you about a website? | It is a website about rivers | *It is a website from Russia | It is a website that only sells food | It is a website for games only
exercise: Find the fragment ru in «February». | feb | *ru | ary | uar
exercise: Which of these is RU a short code for? | *Russia or the Russian language | A football club in London | A famous painter | A type of bread
test: Why is it a good idea to look at the ending of a web address before you click? | *To check where the site is from | To find out the price of the product | To see how many pictures it has | To make the page load faster
test: Is ru a word you can use by itself in a sentence? | Yes, it means Russia | Yes, it means a website ending | Yes, it means Russian language only | *No, it is a fragment, not a word on its own
exam: Which of these best describes ru? | A full sentence about the internet | *A fragment, and also a short code for Russia or the Russian language | A word that means happy | A type of computer program
